                <pb facs="0437" n="347" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg347"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">662.7131/65: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany (Sackett) to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-05-28T16:00:00+01:00">May 28, 1932—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 28—1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>107. Your 57, May 27, 2 p.m. Handed note to Bülow this morning. He expressed keen
                    disappointment and stated that he was not yet able to acquaint me with the
                    attitude of the German Government in the premises.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sackett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
